On Fri, 4 Jan 2007, Tartley wrote:

>  There are files from a game in progress under your name.
>  The files are locked or inaccessible. Is the other game still running?
>  Cannot open I:\Program Files\Nethack\jon-jonathan.0
>
> My docs say that recover is now built into the Nethack exe, and I
> should activate it by running:
>
> Nethack.exe -u<username>
>
> However, running this (using either 'jon' or 'jonathan' as <username>)
> produces the identical message as above, then exits.

You should use "jonathan" while logged on as user "jon".

What does the command
  dir "I:\Program Files\Nethack\jon-jonathan.0"
do? If it says "File Not Found", then a vital part of the recovery
information is lost, and your game cannot be recovered.

> It started up, ate my save game file, produced the 'jon-jonathan.1', etc
> files, and then crashed.

I note that you do not mention a .0-file here...

> Can anyone confirm that recovery using 'nethack.exe' on Windows does
> usually work?

The built-in recovery does usually work, if its data is present.

